		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Parallel simulations]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=26694#p26694"><![CDATA[
Bullet uses instances of simulation worlds for each distinct simulation environment. This hints for the capability of simulating multiple worlds in parallel, given a parallel architecture. However, thread safety is hindered by at least the profiling routines that are very frequent in the code. My question is: How would one go about accomplishing parallel simulation at the world granularity? Are there any other caveats beside profiling that one should look out for?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=9014">kyriazis</a> — Wed Jan 11, 2012 4:54 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
